{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And they were afraid to approach him.</b> Come and see how great is the power of transgression: before they stretched out their hands to transgression, what does Scripture say? ״וּמַרְאֵה כְּבוֹד ה' כְּאֵשׁ אֹכֶלֶת בְּרֹאשׁ הָהָר לְעֵינֵי בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״ (Exodus 24) — and they were neither afraid nor dismayed; but once they made the calf, even the horns of Moses' splendor made them recoil and be dismayed (Sifrei)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:37.454088945Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}